      "content_fixes": [
        {
          "index": 5,
          "old": "And boom, God wrecked the Ethiopians right in front of Asa and the army of Judah. The Ethiopians dipped and ran for their lives. Asa and his crew chased them all the way to Gerar. So many Ethiopians got taken out that they had zero fight left in them—it was a total massacre, courtesy of God and his squad. The soldiers from Judah walked away with tons of loot. They wrecked all the towns around Gerar, where the people were basically paralyzed with fear because of God, and they just plundered the whole area. They also jacked the herdsmen's animals and brought back a crazy amount of sheep and camels to Jerusalem.",
          "new": "And boom, God wrecked the Ethiopians right in front of Asa and the army of Judah. The Ethiopians dipped and ran for their lives. Asa and his crew chased them all the way to Gerar. So many Ethiopians got taken out that they had zero fight left in them—it was a total massacre at the hands of God and his troops. The soldiers from Judah walked away with tons of loot. They wrecked all the towns around Gerar, where the people were basically paralyzed with fear because of God, and they just plundered the whole area. They also jacked the herdsmen's animals and brought back a crazy amount of sheep and camels to Jerusalem.",
